DATA.ielts65.speakModels = [
 {card:'Describe a place you would like to visit.',text:'I’d like to talk about Kyoto in Japan, which I’ve wanted to visit for years. I first heard about it from a documentary about traditional temples and gardens. What attracts me most is the mix of history and nature. For example, I’d love to walk through the bamboo forest and see the old wooden temples, because I think they would be incredibly peaceful. I’d probably go in autumn, when the leaves change colour, and I’d try local food such as tofu dishes. The main reason I want to go is that I enjoy cultures that value calm and tradition, especially since my daily life is very busy. I hope to save enough money within the next two years.'},
 {card:'Describe a time you helped someone.',text:'I’d like to describe the time I helped my cousin prepare for an important exam. She was struggling with English, so I offered to practise with her every evening for a month. We read short articles together and I corrected her pronunciation. At first she was nervous and made lots of mistakes, but gradually she became more confident. In the end, she passed with a good score. I felt really proud, and it also improved my own English because I had to explain things clearly. It taught me that helping others can be rewarding for both people.'},
 {card:'Describe a useful skill you learned.',text:'One skill I’ve found really useful is cooking. I learned it mainly from my grandmother when I was a teenager, and later I practised using online videos. At first my meals were quite bad, but I kept trying and now I can prepare a variety of dishes. The skill is useful because it saves money, and it allows me to eat more healthily than if I bought takeaway food every day. It’s also a good way to relax after work. I think everyone should learn to cook, as it makes you more independent.'}
];
